  "critical": false,
  "description": "Gas turbine engines that convert Brayton cycle shaft power into propulsive thrust via a propeller through a reduction gearbox, achieving higher propulsive efficiency than pure jet engines at subsonic speeds. Combines a turboshaft gas generator core with a multi-stage speed-reducing gear train that steps turbine RPM (20,000-40,000) down to propeller RPM (1,200-2,500). Dominates regional airliners, military transport, maritime patrol, and agricultural aircraft where fuel economy and short-field capability matter more than top speed.",
